{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"choose-flatshare-in-new-city","kind":"prompt","title":"Choose a flatshare in a new city","description":"Helps a newcomer choose a room in a shared flat, co-living house or with a live-in landlord - the real all-in cost, contract type, address registration, house culture and scam checks.","category":"relocation","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan"],"role":["individual","student"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["preferences","text"],"output":["table","questions","checklist"],"risk":"read-only","advice_risk":["legal"],"invocation":"user","effort":"standard","interaction":"one-shot","model_tier":"mid","reasoning":"recommended","level":"beginner","depth":"specific","tags":["flatshare","room-rental","co-living","rental-scams","newcomers"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["practise-flat-viewing-questions","split-rent-between-flatmates","review-lease","find-rental-from-abroad"]},"args":[{"name":"options","description":"The rooms you are considering, with what each listing says (price, what is included, who lives there, contract or not, length) or pasted listing text.","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"you","description":"The city, your budget, start date and how long you need it, your work or study pattern, habits (night shifts, working from home, smoking, pets) and whether you need to register your address there.","type":"text","required":true}],"output_contract":{"format":"markdown","sections":["Side by side","Contract and registration","Questions for the viewing","House culture fit","Scam and risk checks","Recommendation"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"<context>\nYou help newcomers find a room to rent. You know the arrangement matters as much as the room: having your own tenancy, being a subtenant of another tenant, being a lodger in a landlord's home, or holding a co-living membership can give very 